      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOVA CENTAURI (3) started favourite and won two on the trot in strong country sprints then was a shade disappointing at Rosehill nine days ago. Has raced here four times for four wins - big chance to keep that perfect record intact. Stablemate GRANDINI (7) ran on stoutly to finish 1.6 lengths behind NOVA CENTAURI when resuming over 1280m at Muswellbrook last time out. Yet to miss the top three in four second-up runs. Makes plenty of appeal with the light weight. Veteran MACLEAY (6) didn't run a strong 2100m last time so that run can be overlooked. Best form comes at this trip so keep him safe. VALOROUS POWER (2) will probably be better for the run but he has the class to test these if forward enough. ZAMBORGHINI (5) tends to mix his form but a better gate today should see him run well.",
